:: Start
<figure class="scene-media scene-placeholder-only" aria-label="Game Boy screen"><span class="scene-placeholder" aria-hidden="true"></span></figure>
! Neko
//A game about the life of a stray cat.//

Millions of cats live on the streets worldwide. Most were born outside, or were abandoned by people who once called them pets. They are not wild, and they are not safe. Life on the street is often short and difficult:
* ''Hunger:'' Strays rely on scraps, rubbish and occasional kindness. Food is unreliable and often unsafe.
* ''Disease:'' Without vaccines or veterinary care, infections spread easily, especially in winter.
* ''Danger:'' Traffic, cruelty, poison, predators and extreme weather are constant threats.
* ''Fast reproduction:'' One unsterilized female can have multiple litters a year, and many kittens do not survive. This is why sterilization programs are important.

In this game, you ''are'' one of them.
* [[Start|Alley]]

:: Alley
<<scene "alley.mp4" "A city alley">>
! The Alley
You wake up in a narrow alley, with the nasty smell of garbage filling your nose. The past nights were long and cold. Now, the city is waking up around you, but the streets are still quiet. Only the sound of water dripping from the air conditioning in the buildings and the occasional car passing by can be heard.

You're an elegant, <<listbox "$gender">><<option "female">><<option "male">><</listbox>> cat. You lick your <<listbox "$fur">><<option "black">><<option "gray">><<option "orange">><<option "white">><</listbox>> fur clean, stretch and get up. You walk down the alley, and see your <<listbox "$eyes">><<option "green">><<option "yellow">><<option "blue">><<option "gray">><</listbox>> eyes glowing, reflected in a puddle.

Your stomach growls, as you haven't eaten properly in two days. You must find food and water quickly. You also need to be careful, as the city is full of dangers, and not all humans are [[kind|Alley - Leave]].

:: Alley - Leave
<<scene "alley.mp4" "A city alley">>
! The Alley
You start wandering the familiar streets of the quiet city. It's only a matter of time before it starts to get crowded.

While you are getting out of the alley, you notice a red cup with a clear liquid in it. You are feeling thirsty, so you approach it. As your whiskers start touching the water, you notice a strange smell emanating from it. You're not sure it's safe to drink, but you're not really in a position to be picky.

* [[Drink from the cup|Alley - Drink]]
* [[Ignore the cup|Alley - Ignore]]

:: Alley - Drink
<<if not $drinkFromAlley>>
  <<run setup.adjust("health", -1)>>
  <<set $drinkFromAlley to true>>
<</if>>
<<scene "alley.mp4" "A city alley">>
! The Alley
You approach the cup and sniff it. The smell is strange, but you are very thirsty. You decide to take a sip. The liquid tastes bitter and makes you feel dizzy. 

//It was not water, but some kind of alcoholic beverage. It is nasty, and not good for you. (Health -1)//

After a few moments, you feel a bit better, but you are still thirsty. You decide to leave the alley and look for food and water elsewhere. 

You walk a few blocks and see a [[park|Park]] in the distance. 

:: Alley - Ignore
<<scene "alley.mp4" "A city alley">>
! The Alley
You decide it's best if you do not drink from the cup. It smells suspicious, and you don't want to risk it. You decide to leave the alley and look for food and water elsewhere. 

You walk a few blocks and see a [[park|Park]] in the distance. 

:: Park
<<scene "park.gif" "A city park">>
! The Park
You hear the sound of birds chirping in the distance, and you see a few people having a picnic under a tree. You also notice some cats wandering around, looking for food.

A bird is perched on a branch, and it looks like it might be a good meal.

* [[You approach the humans|Park - Humans]]
* [[You approach the bird|Park - Bird]]

:: Park - Humans
<<scene "park.gif" "Humans in the park">>
! The Park
You carefully approach the humans, hoping they might have some food for you. A strong smell of food wafts from their picnic basket. It's a feast!

They notice you and stare for a moment. You're not sure they are friendly.

* [[Steal their food|Park - Steal Food]] 
* [[Meow, pleading for food|Park - Ask for food]]

:: Park - Steal Food
<<if not $stoleParkFood>>
  <<run setup.adjust("hunger", 2)>>
  <<run setup.adjust("trustHumans", -2)>>
  <<set $stoleParkFood to true>>
<</if>>
<<scene "park.gif" "Stealing food from humans">>
! The Park
You wait near the humans, and when they are distracted, you quickly snatch a piece of tuna from their picnic basket. The humans notice you, and they are not happy. With a mouth full of food, you ran as fast as you can, and you manage to escape. 

//You ate well, but your trust in humans has been damaged. (Hunger +2, Trust in Humans -2)//

A light rain starts falling, and you start to feel cold and tired. You need to find a place to rest and warm up. It's time to leave the park.

* [[Explore the city|City]] 
* [[Explore the suburbs|Suburbs]]


:: Park - Ask for food
<<if not $askForParkFood>>
  <<if $fur is "black">>
    <<run setup.adjust("trustHumans", -2)>>
  <<else>>
    <<run setup.adjust("hunger", 2)>>
    <<run setup.adjust("trustHumans", 2)>>
  <</if>>
  <<set $askForParkFood to true>>
<</if>>
<<scene "park.gif" "Asking for food from humans">>
! The Park
<<if $fur is "black">>
  You start meowing and purring at the humans, hoping they will give you some food. They notice you, and they seem scared and uncomfortable. They shoo you away, and you feel disappointed and run away from them.

  //Black cats are often associated with bad luck, and humans are often wary of them. Your trust in humans has been damaged. (Trust in Humans -2)//
<<else>>
You start meowing and purring at the humans, hoping they will give you some food. They notice you, and one of them takes pity on you. They give you a piece of tuna, which you gratefully accept.

//You ate well, and your trust in humans has been shown. (Hunger +2, Trust in Humans +2)//
<</if>>
A light rain starts falling, and you start to feel cold and tired. You need to find a place to rest and warm up. It's time to leave the park.

* [[Explore the city|City]] 
* [[Explore the suburbs|Suburbs]]

:: Park - Bird
<<scene "park.gif" "A bird in the park">>
! The Park
You carefully approach the bird, trying not to make any sudden movements. The bird notices you and starts to fly away into the bushes. You chase after it...

You successfully catch your prey. When you're about to sink your teeth into it, you hear a soft noise behind you. Another cat is watching you from a distance. It seems to be hungry too.

* [[Eat it all|Park - Bird - Eat All]] 
* [[Share it|Park - Bird - Share]]

:: Park - Bird - Eat All
<<if not $eatAllParkBird>>
  <<run setup.adjust("hunger", 3)>>
  <<run setup.adjust("trustCats", -1)>>
  <<set $eatAllParkBird to true>>
<</if>>
<<scene "park.gif" "A bird in the park">>
! The Park
You eat the bird all by yourself, and you feel satisfied. However, the other cat looks disappointed and walks away. You feel a bit guilty for not sharing.

//You ate very well, but your trust in other cats has been damaged. (Hunger +3, Trust in Cats -1)//

A light rain starts falling, and you start to feel cold and tired. You need to find a place to rest and warm up. It's time to leave the park.

* [[Explore the city|City]] 
* [[Explore the suburbs|Suburbs]]

:: Park - Bird - Share
<<if not $shareParkBird>>
  <<run setup.adjust("hunger", 2)>>
  <<run setup.adjust("trustCats", 2)>>
  <<set $shareParkBird to true>>
<</if>>
<<scene "park.gif" "A bird in the park">>
! The Park
You decide to let the other cat get close to you, and you share the bird with it. In a world where food is scarce, sharing is a risk that can also be rewarding. The other cat seems grateful, and grooms you as a sign of trust.

//You ate well, and your trust in other cats has been shown. (Hunger +2, Trust in Cats +2)//

A light rain starts falling, and you start to feel cold and tired. You need to find a place to rest and warm up. You decide to leave the park.

* [[Explore the city|City]] 
* [[Explore the suburbs|Suburbs]]

:: Suburbs
<<scene "suburbs.gif" "The suburbs">>
! The Suburbs
Reaching the suburbs, you notice that the streets are more quiet and less crowded. The houses are bigger, and there are more trees and gardens. It has stopped raining, however, the ground is wet and muddy. A cold breeze is blowing.

You spot what looks like a squirrel in a tree. Instinctively, you start to chase it, but it quickly runs away. Before you're able to catch your breath, you hear a noise. It's a soft rustling in the bushes.

The sound of a branch breaking behind you makes you turn around. A dog is running towards you, barking loudly. You need to find a way to [[escape|Suburbs - Dog]].

:: Suburbs - Dog
<<if not $runFromDog>>
  <<run setup.adjust("hunger", -2)>>
  <<run setup.adjust("health", -2)>>
  <<set $runFromDog to true>>
<</if>>
<<scene "suburbs-alley.gif" "The suburbs">>
! The Suburbs
After a long chase, you manage to escape the dog. You find yourself in a quiet street. Perhaps it's time to leave the Suburbs.

//Running from the dog has left you exhausted and hungry. You feel weak and tired. (Health -2, Hunger -2)//

However, before you head out, you see a puddle of water on the ground, and it triggers the instinct to drink it. The puddle seems perfect to quench your thirst.

* [[Leave the suburbs|Suburbs - City]] 
* [[Drink from the puddle|Water - Puddle]]

:: Suburbs - City
<<if not $runFromDogToCity>>
  <<run setup.adjust("hunger", 1)>>
  <<run setup.adjust("health", 1)>>
  <<set $runFromDogToCity to true>>
<</if>>
<<scene "suburbs.gif" "The suburbs">>
! The Suburbs
You decided to leave the Suburbs. Luckily, you found a soggy piece of bread on the floor, and a puddle of rain water, which were just enough to keep you going. It starts lightly raining again, as you head to the [[city|City]].

//Eating the bread and drinking water has given you some energy. (Health +1, Hunger +1)//

:: Water - Puddle
<<scene "suburbs-alley.gif" "The suburbs">>
! The Suburbs 
You drink from the puddle, and you feel a bit better. You find a few bushes to hide in, and you rest for a while. You fall asleep listening to the wind [[blowing...|Ending-Poisoned]]

:: Ending-Poisoned
<<if not $endingPoisoned>>
  <<run setup.adjust("health", -10)>>
  <<set $endingPoisoned to true>>
<</if>>
<<scene "suburbs.gif" "The suburbs">>
! The Suburbs
And the next time you wake up, you feel weak and dizzy. The puddle was poisoned with pesticides.

You try to find help, but you can't. You feel your body shutting down, and you know that this is the end. You were a stray cat, and your life was hard.

//Stray cats drink from puddles, drains and garages, and eat from bins, so they meet poisons more often than pets do. Antifreeze tastes sweet and is extremely toxic: a very small amount can be fatal. Rat poison can also kill cats that eat a poisoned rodent.//

//Cats hide illness, so by the time symptoms show, it is often too late. Nobody knows how many die this way, because most deaths are never recorded.//

* [[Credits|Credits]]

:: City
<<scene "citycrowded.gif" "City">>
<<if not $cityCold>>
  <<run setup.adjust("health", -1)>>
  <<set $cityCold to true>>
<</if>>
! The City
You enter the heart of the city. After a long walk through the crowded streets, you find yourself noticing a certain weight on your fur. The rain has become snow. You sneeze. The cold is starting to get to you.

//The cold makes you feel weak. (Health -1)//

Searching for a shelter has become urgent. There are lights, sounds and movements all around you. The city is fully awake, and the streets are crowded with people and cars. You're afraid.

Suddenly, you start smelling a delicious, warm and fishy aroma. It leads to a nearby restaurant. At the same time, you notice a train station, which could be a good place to find shelter. You also see a road that leads to the suburbs, where you might find a quieter place to rest. So many choices... Where should you go?

* [[Go to the restaurant|Restaurant]]
* [[Enter the train station|Train Station]]
* [[Keep exploring the city|City - Road]] 

:: Restaurant
<<scene "restaurant.gif" "Restaurant">>
! The Restaurant
//Sniff sniff// You follow the smell of fried fish and find yourself in front of a restaurant. The scent is overflowing your mind, as you imagine yourself eating a big, juicy piece of fish, and your stomach growls in anticipation.

* [[Go around to the back of the restaurant|Restaurant - Back]]
* [[Stay around the entrance|Restaurant - Front]]

:: Restaurant - Back
<<scene "restaurant.gif" "Restaurant">>
! The Restaurant
You walk around, trying to locate where the tasty smell is coming from. Eventually, you find and go down the alley that leads to the back of the restaurant. One of the white-uniform humans comes outside to take out the trash. As you approach the trash to look for scraps, he notices you.

* [[You hide from him|Restaurant - Trash]]
* [[You let him approach you|Restaurant - Worker]]


:: Restaurant - Worker
<<if not $workerPetYou>>
  <<run setup.adjust("trustHumans", +1)>>  
  <<set $workerPetYou to true>>
<</if>>
<<scene "restaurant.gif" "Restaurant">>
! The Restaurant
He briefly pets you and then goes inside for a moment.

//You feel a bit nervous, but you enjoy the attention and care. (Trust in Humans +1)//

* [[You wait for him|Restaurant - Worker - Food]]
* [[You go back to the trash|Restaurant - Trash]]

:: Restaurant - Worker - Food
<<if not $workerFedYou>>
  <<run setup.adjust("hunger", +3)>>
  <<run setup.adjust("trustHumans", +2)>>  
  <<set $workerFedYou to true>>
<</if>>
<<scene "restaurant.gif" "Restaurant">>
! The Restaurant
The human comes back with a plate with pieces of fish and skin. He puts it down on the ground, gets up, and lights his cigarette. He starts puffing the smoke, looking at you.

You quickly scrap the last bits of fish, and lick your lips. 

//You feel very satisfied. You also feel that, maybe, humans aren't so bad after all. (Hunger +3, Trust in Humans +2)//

With your belly full, you start feeling sleepy. There are a few cardboard boxes and wooden crates around, and you find a covered spot to curl up and rest. You feel safe for now. Your eyes are getting heavy, and you drift off to [[sleep...|Human - Cage]].

:: Restaurant - Trash
<<if not $eatFromRestaurantTrash>>
  <<run setup.adjust("hunger", +1)>>
  <<run setup.adjust("health", -1)>>  
  <<set $eatFromRestaurantTrash to true>>
<</if>>
<<scene "restaurant.gif" "Restaurant">>
! The Restaurant
You hide from him and wait a little bit. As your stomach growls, you go to the trash he just threw away and start rummaging through it. You find some scraps of food, but they are not enough to fill your belly.  

//You eat nasty food scraps from the trash. It is not tasty, but it is better than nothing. (Hunger +1, Health -1)//

It's been a long day. In this alley, you find a cardboard box to curl up in and rest. You feel safe for now. Your eyes are getting heavy, and you drift off to [[sleep...|Human - Cage]].

:: Restaurant - Front
<<scene "restaurant.gif" "Restaurant">>
! The Restaurant
People with big, fancy, furry coats are coming in and going out the restaurant's front doors. They seem busy, and you don't want to get in their way. You look inside through the glass windows, and you see people dressed in white uniforms carrying metal trays, some with food, some covered in cloches.

After a while, some people notice you and start getting closer. You're not sure if they are friendly or not. You have to make a decision quickly.

* [[Let them get close|Restaurant - Front - Pet]]
* [[Run away|Restaurant - Back]]

:: Restaurant - Front - Pet
<<if not $frontPetYou>>
  <<run setup.adjust("trustHumans", +1)>>  
  <<set $frontPetYou to true>>
<</if>>
<<scene "restaurant.gif" "Restaurant">>
! The Restaurant
These humans are friendly, and they start petting you. After a few minutes of snuggling, they end up leaving. Petting feels nice but it does not fill your belly.

//You feel a bit nervous, but you enjoy the attention. (Trust in Humans +1)//

You decide to follow the strong smell of food, coming from the [[side alley of the restaurant|Restaurant - Back]].

:: Train Station
<<if not $sleepInTrainStation>>
  <<run setup.adjust("hunger", -2)>>  
  <<set $sleepInTrainStation to true>>
<</if>>
<<scene "trainstation.gif" "Train Station">>
! The Train Station
Last night you were so tired you don't even remember falling asleep. Apparently, you spent the night in the train station, and you wake up to the sound of trains passing by.

//You wake up feeling hungry. (Hunger -2)//

Water is still falling from the sky, although you feel warmer today. You stretch, groom yourself, and start walking around the station. There are a few humans around, some are sitting on benches, others are running around. Strange [[creatures|Train Station - Cat or Humans]] they are. 

:: Train Station - Cat or Humans
<<scene "trainstation.gif" "Train Station">>
! The Train Station
After wandering for a while, you find another cat, who seems to be a stray like you. It looks at you and meows. You meow back. The black, skinny cat seems to understand you.

It looks like the cat lives in the station. Humans are kind enough to pet and feed it. Perhaps they will be nice to you too. Who should you go meet?

* [[Meet the humans|Train Station - Humans]]
* [[Meet the cat|Train Station - Cat]]

:: Train Station - Cat
<<if not $metCatInTrainStation>>
  <<run setup.adjust("trustCats", +1)>>  
  <<set $metCatInTrainStation to true>>
<</if>>
<<scene "cat-station.gif" "Train Station">>
! The Train Station
You approach the other cat, perhaps a new friend. As you get close to the furry stranger, it seems to be a bit wary of you. You meow and purr, trying to show that you mean no harm. The other cat seems to understand you, and it starts to purr back. You feel a sense of relief and happiness, as you have found a new friend in this strange place. 

//You realize that you are not alone in this world, and that there are other cats out there who are also struggling to survive. (Trust in Cats +1)//

The other cat seems to have a small shelter and bowls for food and water. This could mean that humans are kind enough to feed it. Should you stay and share the food with the other cat, or should you go meet the humans and see if they will feed you too?

* [[Leave the cat and meet the humans|Train Station - Humans]]
* [[Stay with the cat|Train Station - Cat - Part 2]]

:: Train Station - Cat - Part 2
<<if not $eatFromCatInTrainStation>>
  <<run setup.adjust("trustCats", +1)>>  
  <<run setup.adjust("hunger", +1)>>  
  <<set $eatFromCatInTrainStation to true>>
<</if>>
<<scene "cat-station.gif" "Train Station">>
! The Train Station
You decide to stay with your new furry friend. After all, it is good to have someone have your back in this world. The cat seems to be a permanent resident of the station. Humans regularly feed him. He lets you have a little bit of his food and water. It isn't much, but it is enough to keep you going.

//You feel happy and grateful for the food and water, and to have found a friend in this strange place. (Hunger +1, Trust in Cats +1)//

You both become close. You groom each other, and you keep each other company. You feel a sense of belonging and companionship that you haven't felt in a long [[time...|Train Station - Cat - Part 3]]

:: Train Station - Cat - Part 3
<<if not $feelWeakInStation>>
  <<run setup.adjust("health", -2)>>  
  <<set $feelWeakInStation to true>>
<</if>>
<<scene "cat-station.gif" "Train Station">>
! The Train Station
At first everything seems to be going well. You and your new friend are surviving together. However, as time passes by, you start feeling sick and weak. 

//You feel very weak and tired. You don't know what is happening to you, or what caused you to feel this way. (Health -2)//

As you interact with your friend, you realize that you are not the only one who is affected. You are both feeling [[weak...|Train Station - Cat - Part 4]]

:: Train Station - Cat - Part 4
<<set $hasFelv to true>>
<<scene "cat-station-night.gif" "Train Station">>
! The Train Station
//The other cat is sick with Feline Leukemia Virus (FeLV). You were also infected with the virus, as it is spread by sharing food, bitting, grooming, and other close contact.//

FeLV is a serious disease that affects cats, and it can be [[fatal.|Train Station - Cat - Part 5]]

:: Train Station - Cat - Part 5
<<scene "cat-station-night.gif" "Train Station">>
! The Train Station
Eventually, a short, middle-aged human passing by the station notices you and your friend. You both have had better days.

She seems to be studying you, although you are not sure why. You feel she may not be trustworthy...

After looking at both of you for a while, she comes in your friend's direction, looking like she might want to hurt him. He also notices her and, just as she is about to grab him, he manages to escape. It all happened so fast, you are not sure what to do.

She scoffs, and turns to you.

* [[You run from her|Train Station - Ending - Disease]]
* [[You let her get close|Train Station - Veterinary]]

:: Train Station - Veterinary
<<scene "cat-station-night.gif" "Train Station">>
! The Train Station
You feel too weak to run, so you let her get close. The human picks you up and puts you in a cage. All of this makes you feel even more vulnerable. You feel scared and confused, try to meow and escape, but to no [[avail...|Sterilization]]

:: Train Station - Ending - Disease
<<run setup.adjust("health", -10)>>  
<<scene "cat-station-night.gif" "Train Station">>
! The Train Station
You used your last bit of energy to try to escape. After just a few moments, you realize you are too weak to continue. You end up collapsing, nearby the station, feeling your body shut down.

You were a stray cat, and your life was hard. You were a survivor, but in the end, you couldn't overcome the dangers of the streets. Feline Leukemia Virus (FeLV) is a serious disease that weakens a cat's immune system, so ordinary infections become deadly. Without veterinary care, a stray has almost no chance of fighting it.

//FeLV spreads through saliva and close contact: grooming each other, sharing bowls, fights, and from mother to kittens. Many infected cats look healthy for a long time, so the virus can spread unnoticed in a colony.//

//Nobody knows how many strays die from it, because most deaths are never recorded or tested.//

* [[Credits|Credits]]

:: Train Station - Humans
<<if not $eatFromHumansInTrainStation>>
  <<run setup.adjust("hunger", +1)>>  
  <<run setup.adjust("trustHumans", +1)>>
  <<set $eatFromHumansInTrainStation to true>>
<</if>>
<<scene "trainstation.gif" "Train Station">>
! The Train Station
The humans are kind enough to pet and feed the other cat. So you assume they should be kind to you too. You approach them, and they notice you and pet you. After interacting with a few of the tall humans, one one of them decides to feed you. 

//You feel happy and satisfied. (Hunger +1, Trust in Humans +1)//

Perhaps, humans aren't so bad [[after all|Train Station - Humans - Part 2]].

:: Train Station - Humans - Part 2
<<if not $trainStationHumans2>>
  <<run setup.adjust("hunger", -1)>>  
  <<set $trainStationHumans2 to true>>
<</if>>
<<scene "trainstation.gif" "Train Station">>
! The Train Station
You end up spending a few days in the train station, and you feel safe and cared for. You have a roof over your head, which makes you feel secure. However, food is never a guarantee. Some days you are lucky, and some days you are not...

//The last few days have not been too bad, but you are not eating very well. (Hunger -1)//

* [[Stay in the train station|Train Station - Stay]]
* [[Leave the train station|Train Station - Leave]]

:: Train Station - Leave
<<scene "trainstation.gif" "Train Station">>
! The Train Station
Leaving the train station is a hard decision, but your instincts tell you that you need to keep moving. You head into the city, and you find yourself in a busy street. The familiar scent of warm food is back and, this time, you decide to [[follow it|Restaurant]].

:: Train Station - Stay
<<if not $stayInTrainStation>>
  <<run setup.adjust("hunger", -2)>>  
  <<run setup.adjust("health", -1)>>  
  <<set $stayInTrainStation to true>>
<</if>>
<<scene "trainstation.gif" "Train Station">>
! The Train Station
As days pass, you decide to stay in the station. After all, it is a safe place, and the closest to a home you have ever felt.

However, you are skinnier by the day. You never know when a piece of food will come your way, and you are always [[hungry...|Train Station - Stay - Part 2]]

//The lack of proper nutrition is also affecting your health. (Hunger -2, Health -1)//

:: Train Station - Stay - Part 2
<<if not $stayInTrainStation2>>
  <<run setup.adjust("hunger", -2)>>  
  <<run setup.adjust("health", -1)>>  
  <<set $stayInTrainStation2 to true>>
<</if>>
<<scene "trainstation.gif" "Train Station">>
! The Train Station
You feel weak and more vulnerable by the day. 

//The lack of proper nutrition is also affecting your health. (Hunger -2, Health -1)//
<<if $health lte 2>>
As you stare at the less crowded station, you fear this might be the end. You keep trying to find a way to get food, but you are too [[weak|Train Station - Ending - Hunger]] to even plead.
<<else>>
You still feel that you have strength, and although leaving the train station is a hard decision, your instincts tell you that you need to keep moving. You head into the city, and you find yourself in a busy street. The familiar scent of warm food is back and, this time, you decide to [[follow it|Restaurant]].
<</if>>

:: Train Station - Ending - Hunger
<<run setup.adjust("hunger", -10)>>  
<<scene "trainstation.gif" "Train Station">>
! The Train Station
You were a stray cat, and your life was hard. You were a survivor, but in the end, you couldn't overcome the dangers of the streets. Hunger is one of the biggest threats to stray cats. Relying on scraps, rubbish and occasional kindness, food is unreliable and often unsafe. Many stray cats die from starvation, especially in winter.

//Free-roaming cats face starvation, extreme weather, predators and disease. The more cats there are in one place, the more they compete for food, and the fewer kittens survive.//

//Nobody knows how many strays die of hunger, because most deaths are never recorded.//

* [[Credits|Credits]]

:: City - Road
<<if not $cityRoadCold>>
  <<run setup.adjust("health", -1)>>  
  <<set $cityRoadCold to true>>
<</if>>
<<scene "citycrowded.gif" "City">>
! The City
You decide to keep exploring the city. There are cars passing, trucks making noise getting the snow out of the road, people in big coats rushing... Lots of activity all around you. You feel a bit scared, but you keep moving forward. The snow is falling heavily, and you feel even colder than before. You need to hurry up and find a place to rest and warm up.

//The cold of the snow makes you feel even weaker. (Health -1)//

Someone steps on your tail, and you feel a sharp pain. You yelp in pain, but nobody notices. You try to run away, crossing the [[road...|Road - Runover]]

:: Road - Runover
<<scene "citycrowded.gif" "City">>
! The City
Suddenly, a car is coming towards you, and you can't get out of the way in time. The cold and icy road makes it hard for the driver to break in time.

You try to dodge, but your body is too slow and stiff from the cold. You see a strong light approaching, and then everything goes [[black|Ending - Runover]].

:: Ending - Runover
<<scene "citycrowded.gif" "City">>
! The City

//The real number of stray cats killed on the road is unknown. However, studies of free-roaming pet cats show how dangerous roads are. Road accidents are the most common cause of death in cats, and especially for kittens.//

//In Europe, an estimated 1 in 5 free-roaming cats is hit by a car during its life, and most of those accidents are fatal.//

* [[Credits|Credits]]

:: Human - Cage
<<scene "restaurant.gif" "City">>
! The restaurant
You suddenly wake up with a human picking you up. You feel a bit scared, but have no time to react. The human puts inside you a cage. Under your body, you feel a soft blanket. It's comforting, but you're still scared and confused. You try to meow and escape, but to no [[avail...|Sterilization]]

:: Sterilization
<<if not $arrivedAtSterilization>>
  <<run setup.adjust("hunger", +1)>>  
  <<set $arrivedAtSterilization to true>>
<</if>>
<<scene "clinic.gif" "City">>
! The Clinic
You feel dizzy and scared as they carry you for what feels like an eternity, and then they take you inside a room. There are different voices and noises outside, which keep you on alert. You don't know what is happening...

Eventually, someone comes to you, opens the cage, and softly touches you. They carefully offer you some food and water. At first, you are afraid to leave the cage where they put you, but your stomach is growling, and you decide to eat.

//You feel a bit better after eating, but you are still scared and confused. (Hunger +1)//

After a while, the humans come back. They pick you up, touch you and sting you. You still don't understand what is happening. Before you notice, you're back in the [[cage.|Sterilization - Part2]]

:: Sterilization - Part2
<<scene "clinic.gif" "City">>
! The Clinic
You wake up suddenly with someone entering the room. A human comes in and takes you.

They sting you again. You start to feel [[sleepy...|Sterilization - Part3]]

:: Sterilization - Part3
<<if not $sterilized3>>
  <<run setup.adjust("health", +3)>>  
  <<set $sterilized3 to true>>
<</if>>
<<scene "clinic.gif" "City">>
! The Clinic
Finally, you wake up, slowly. You feel dizzy once again, and in some pain. What has happened...?

//Strangely, there is a feeling of relief. You feel taken care of. (Health +3)//

A few days go by... You are once again taken to another place. At this point you're getting used to this routine. At least you have food, and you're not cold [[anymore...|Shelter]]

:: Shelter
<<scene "shelter.gif" "City">>
! The Shelter
This time, you're in a louder place. You hear dogs barking, cats meowing, and other noises. You are put in a room with other cats.

<<if $runFromDog is true>>\
Hearing the dogs outside stresses you out, as you remember the last time you were chased by one. You feel a bit scared, but you are not alone.

<</if>>\
<<if $hasFelv is true>>\
You were tested for Feline Leukemia Virus (FeLV), and the results came back positive. You are put in a separate room with other infected [[cats|Shelter - FeLV]].
<<elseif $trustCats gt $trustHumans>>\
Since you are used to being around other cats, you feel happy to have some company. You start to play with the other cats, and you feel a sense of [[belonging|Shelter - Colony]].
<<elseif $trustCats lt $trustHumans>>\
Since you are not used to being around other cats, you feel a bit uncomfortable. You try to avoid the other cats, you don't know if they are friendly or [[not|Shelter - Adopted]].
<<else>>\
The other cats watch you, and the humans watch you from the other side of the door. Nobody pushes you either way: the choice is yours.
* [[Join the other cats|Shelter - Colony]]
* [[Approach the humans|Shelter - Adopted]]
<</if>>

:: Shelter - Adopted
<<scene "shelter.gif" "City">>
! The Shelter
After some time in the shelter, you realize humans sometimes come and visit the cats. Sometimes they take one, and sometimes they simply leave.

One day, a small human comes and notices you. You approach her and she pets you. She looks at the other humans and points at you. You sense a connection, and they take you [[home.|Adopted]]

:: Adopted
<<scene "adopted.webp" "City">>
! Adopted
They take you to a warm house, and give you food and water. You feel happy and safe. You are now a pet, and you have a family that loves you.

You are one of the lucky ones.

//In Portugal's official collection centers, about 40,000 dogs and cats arrived in 2025, and about 22,000 were adopted. Many others are never taken in at all: a national census counted over 830,000 stray cats in mainland Portugal.//

//Adoption saves a life, and it also makes space for the next animal. Microchipped, sterilized cats are also much easier to return to their families if they get lost.//

* [[Credits|Credits]]

:: Shelter - Colony
<<scene "colony.jpg" "City">>
! The Colony
In the streets, you were used to being around other cats. You helped and asked for help. Now, you are part of a family of many like you. You are sterilized, have food, water and a warm place to sleep.

You survived the difficult life of the streets, and can live a happy life in the colony.

//Colonies managed with the capture, sterilize and return method stop the cycle of endless litters, and the cats stay in their territory. Many municipalities now fund these programmes, but they depend on volunteers who feed and care for the cats every day.//

//In 2025, Portuguese official centers performed more than 43,000 sterilizations, but experts still say more investment is needed.//

* [[Credits|Credits]]

:: Shelter - FeLV
<<scene "shelter.gif" "City">>
! The Shelter
You end up having a normal life in the shelter. You are among others like you, that never end up having a family, as humans are usually scared to adopt them.

//Feline leukemia (FeLV) does not mean a cat is suffering. Many positive cats live comfortably for years with good care, but the virus can spread to other cats through close contact, so they need a home without non-infected cats, or a shelter that separates them.//

//There is a vaccine, and testing new cats is the first step. Most shelters report that older cats and cats with medical needs wait the longest for a home.//

* [[Credits|Credits]]

:: Credits
<<scene "cat.gif" "Credits">>
! Credits

Thanks for playing Neko. This game was made to raise awareness about the life of stray cats, and the dangers they face every day.

